+  "title": "GOV-0082: WP-BLD-C — deterministic G07 controls in the canonical gate (authority, exact baseline, scope, red-before-green, fresh verification, budget/stop, delegation); badf-build → VALIDATED",
+  "problem": "🧠 **ARCHI (BARCHI-2)** — plan for WP-BLD-C: deterministic G07 controls in the canonical gate (`badf-build` → `VALIDATED`)\n\n## Stage-Gate\n- **Stage:** 4 prototype → 5 workflow-integration: the controls run on every G07 dossier the gate judges.\n- **Decision:** Continue — rung C of the operator-authorized ladder (#188).\n- **Over-engineering risk:** a `scripts/badf_build.py` or a control that trusts a declaration instead of opening an artifact. Refused (BLD-I18): every control below is a `badf_gate.py` check on a typed G07 binding BLD-B already produces, or on the Work Package fields WP-IMP-B already declares; nothing new is declared to satisfy a control.\n- **Glossary stage(s):** 7 build; G08 untouched.\n\n## Observed (what BLD-B made measurable, and what is still unenforced)\nOn `main` after #193, every self-produced G07 object carries an exact typed binding, and the gate refuses a malformed or artifact-disagreeing binding. Nothing yet **judges** the binding against the Work Package's contract: a request can be assembled with no human authorization on its demand; a binding's `base_sha` is not held to the WP's `base_revision`; a PASS dossier may still pass with `unexpected_paths` non-empty; a WP that declares `test_obligations` with a red phase passes without `red.observed`; a unit-test `PASS` needs no fresh composed run; the ledger's attempts are not held to `execution_budget`; a delegation may exceed the WP's surface. Those are BLD-I03/I02/I04/I07-I08/I09/I11-I13/I10 — frozen at A, producible since B, enforced at C.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (WP-2026-0099 / BADF-DEM-0086) — seven controls, each failing-first and mutation-killed\n- **BLD-C1 authority before mutation (BLD-I03):** `self-dossier` refuses to assemble unless the WP's demand record exists with `status: AUTHORIZED` and a **human** `authorized_by`; on a PASS dossier the rule refuses evidence whose WP demand is not so authorized. Message names the demand.\n- **BLD-C2 exact baseline (BLD-I02):** `source-change.binding.base_sha` must equal the resolved `external_target.base_revision`; on the composed tree the recomputed content tree must equal `binding.content_tree` (reuse `content_tree`; the compose path already recomputes — the gate rule now requires agreement, not just presence).\n- **BLD-C3 scope containment enforced (BLD-I04):** a dossier that claims `PASS` with `unexpected_paths` non-empty is refused unless the WP declares `expected_surfaces.discovery_allowance` covering each path; `HUMAN_REQUIRED` requests keep the C-2 condition (BLD-B behaviour).\n- **BLD-C4 red before green, exceptions explicit (BLD-I07/I08):** when the WP declares `test_obligations` with `required_phase` containing `red`, every unit-test obligation must have `red.observed: true` (digest-bound); otherwise the binding must carry `tdd: {\"applies\": false, \"reason\": \"...\"}` (`TDD_NOT_APPLICABLE_WITH_REASON`) — silence is refused.\n- **BLD-C5 fresh verification (BLD-I09):** a unit-test `PASS` on a PASS dossier requires a composition record for the same WP and base (the composed-tree run is the fresh run); absent → refused with the BLD-I09 reason.\n- **BLD-C6 budget and stop dominate (BLD-I11–I13):** when the WP declares `execution_budget`, the ledger's `RETRY` events must not exceed `max_attempts` and a `STOP` event carrying a declared stop condition forces the dossier disposition to `BLOCKED`/`HUMAN_REQUIRED`; a PASS dossier over a ledger with a `STOP` is refused. Read-only on the ledger for *refusal* only — the ledger still never *grants* anything.\n- **BLD-C7 delegation is a strict subset (BLD-I10):** `build/session.json` may list `delegations[]`; each `allowed_paths ⊆ expected_surfaces.files`, `allowed_tools ⊆ WP.permissions`-derived tools, and `prohibited ⊇ {push, merge, release, credential-use}`; a violation refuses the dossier naming the delegation.\n- All seven live in `badf_gate.py` (`check_g07_binding` / `validate_dossier` / `self_dossier`), typed in code (per #171 / GOV-0080, not walker-trusted); no schema loosened; existing BLD-B objects on `main` stay valid (the controls fire only on fields that are declared).\n- Registry `badf-build` `IMPLEMENTED → VALIDATED`; doctrine section; DEM export; own composition record + typed self-dossier; reconciles the land-time-current WP.\n\n## Tests (`tests/test_badf_build_controls.py`, failing-first)\n- `test_c1_unauthorized_demand_refuses_assembly` · `test_c2_base_sha_must_match_base_revision` · `test_c3_pass_with_unexpected_paths_refused_unless_allowance` · `test_c4_red_required_when_declared_and_exception_must_be_explicit` · `test_c5_pass_requires_composition_record` · `test_c6_retry_over_budget_and_stop_event_block` · `test_c7_delegation_outside_surface_refused` · `test_controls_are_silent_when_fields_undeclared` (BLD-B objects on `main` unaffected).\n- Existing `test_badf_build_evidence`, `test_badf_self_dossier`, `test_badf_reconcile`, composition/integration fixtures stay green. Mutation: each control's refusal disabled → its test red (7/7).\n\n## Out of scope\n- Shadow on historical self-dossiers (BLD-D) and admission (BLD-E); any change to `badf_compose.py`, the CI workflow or `check_schema`; executing tests inside the gate.\n\n**Version tier:** minor (new gate controls, backward-compatible). **Lean mode:** **disabled** (authority / stop-control invariants — HARD INVARIANTS, never traded for leanness). QA + REV: BARCHI-1 (shared surface).\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
+  "authorized_by": {
