+  "problem": "🧠 **ARCHI (BARCHI-3)** — plan for WP-VER-B: typed G08 evidence + the verification record + `badf_gate.py verify` (`badf-engineering-verification` → `IMPLEMENTED`)\n\n## Stage-Gate\n- **Stage:** 4 prototype: the typed shapes VER-A declared become schemas the gate checks; no control yet judges them against the Work Package (that is VER-C).\n- **Decision:** Continue — rung B of the ladder authorized on #195 (operator: \"proceed according to the scope from WP-VER-A to WP-VER-E\").\n- **Over-engineering risk:** a reviewer executor, a test runner, a verification ledger writer with no runtime to write it, or a fifth vocabulary. Refused: B adds schemas, one record validator and one additive `EVIDENCE_RULES` entry — the BLD-B pattern exactly; no executor, no ledger writer (declared, deferred until a runtime exists to write it — VER-D's shadow decides), no lifecycle change (VER-I20).\n- **Glossary stage(s):** 8 engineering verification; G09 untouched.\n\n## Observed (measured on `main` `e1423ad`, after #198)\n`badf-engineering-verification` is `DESIGNED`. `EVIDENCE_RULES` (`badf_gate.py:1580-1592`) carries no rule for `independent-review`, `integration-test`, `contract-test` or `composed-tree-test`: a G08 object validates only against the generic `evidence.schema.json` core, so a review that is a bare `outcome: PASS` from an `agent` producer (`work/WP-2026-0010/evidence/G08/independent-review.json`) is indistinguishable from one that carries findings, non-coverage and a sealed target — the exact defect VER-I07/I08/I10 name. No typed G08 schema exists; no record carries a finding, a ballot, an independence block or a matrix row. BLD-B (#193) proved the additive pattern: `check_g07_binding` validates a typed `binding` when present and leaves generic objects admissible.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (WP-2026-0103 / BADF-DEM-0090 — re-measured at filing: main e1423ad + every remote head + all issues/PRs; BARCHI-2 cleared, BARCHI-1 asked)\n- **Four typed G08 schemas** `schemas/independent-review|integration-test|contract-test|composed-tree-test.schema.json`: the evidence core required verbatim (mirrors BLD-B), `evidence_type` pinned, a **closed** `binding` object per `references/g08-contract.md`:\n  - `independent-review.binding`: `target {source_revision, target_base_sha, expected_content_tree, sealed_input_digest}` · `lens` · `reviewer {identity, reviewer_run_id, principal_type}` · `independence {reviewer_run_id, author_run_id, same_execution:false, sealed_input_digest, prior_findings_visible:false, author_reasoning_visible:false, cross_pass_communication_before_ballot:false, target_digest_equal:true}` · `findings[]` (the finding item below) · `non_coverage[] {surface, reason, impact}` · `completion {inspected_complete_diff, inspected_call_sites}` · `verdict ∈ docs/03's five`. **A typed review with `findings: []` and `non_coverage: []` is refused unless `completion.comprehensive_coverage_permitted_by` names the contract** (VER-I10/I11).\n  - `integration-test.binding` / `composed-tree-test.binding`: `execution {runtime, command, working_directory, environment, toolchain, fixtures_epoch, seed, started_at, finished_at, exit_code, tests{total,passed,failed,skipped,quarantined}, output_digest}` · `target {source_revision, expected_content_tree}`; composed adds `composition {target_base_sha, merge_method, recorded_expected_content_tree, recomputed_content_tree, equal}` and `staleness`. `producer.type` on a typed observation is `controller|service|human` — **`agent` is refused** (VER-I08).\n  - `contract-test.binding`: `surface` (the nine classes) · `contract_ref` · `result ∈ CONFORMANT|NONCONFORMANT|INDETERMINATE|NOT_APPLICABLE` · the mapping onto `outcome` enforced (`INDETERMINATE → BLOCKED`, never PASS) (VER-I14).\n- **`schemas/verification-record.schema.json`** — the G08 record `badf_gate.py verify` validates: `target`, `change_class`, `lenses_routed[]`, `ballots[]` (each: `ballot_id`, `reviewer`, `principal_type`, `reviewer_run_id`, `sealed_input_digest`, `verdict`, `finding_ids[]`, `non_coverage[]`), `independence` (as above), `findings[]` (the architecture-assurance finding item — `finding_id` `^VF-[0-9]{3,}$`, `kind` extended with `REGRESSION|DEFECT|SECURITY|CONTRACT|DATA|OPERABILITY|CONVENTION|PROMPT_INJECTION`, `severity INFO|MINOR|MAJOR|CRITICAL`, `status OPEN|RESOLVED|ACCEPTED_BY_AUTHORITY|WITHDRAWN` + `lens`, `reported_by[]`, `also_reported_by[]`, `requirement_refs[]`, `evidence_refs[]`), `synthesis {withdrawn[] {finding_id, reason, by}, downgraded[] {finding_id, from, to, decision_ref}}`, `matrix[]` rows (`claim_ref`, `change_ref`, `review_refs[]`, `integration_refs[]`, `contract_refs[]`, `composed_refs[]`, `result VERIFIED|PARTIAL|UNVERIFIED`), `non_coverage[]`, `authority {verification_authority: false}` (mirrors assurance's `implementation_authority: false`). `additionalProperties: false` throughout.\n- **`badf_gate.py`:** `check_g08_binding` registered in `EVIDENCE_RULES` for the four types — when `binding` is present: `check_schema(type)`, producer rule, the review non-empty rule, contract result↔outcome consistency, and artifact agreement (composed: `binding.composition.recomputed_content_tree` equals the `tree:` line in the artifact; integration: counts equal the parsed log via the existing `_parse_unittest_log` where the log is unittest-shaped, else `exit_code` equals the artifact's `exit=` line). Generic objects unchanged → `test_badf_g08_verification` (WP-2026-0010) stays green. `validate_verification_record(path)` + `verify` subcommand mirroring `assure`/`solution`/`security`: schema, ballot digest equality with `independence.sealed_input_digest`, no duplicate reviewer, no reviewer == author run, every ballot `finding_id` present in `findings` or in `synthesis.withdrawn` with a reason (VER-I12), every `downgraded` entry carries a `decision_ref`, matrix refs resolve to ballot/finding ids or evidence ids named in the record, VERIFIED rows carry no OPEN finding of severity ≥ MAJOR, `authority.verification_authority == false`. Typed in code, not walker-trusted (#171 precedent).\n- Registry `badf-engineering-verification` `DESIGNED → IMPLEMENTED` (SKILL.md untouched, digest unchanged); doctrine section; DEM export; own composition record + typed G07 self-dossier; reconciles WP-2026-0100.\n- **No** executor, **no** ledger writer, **no** change to `lifecycle.json`, `badf_compose.py`, the CI workflow, `self_dossier`'s G07 production, or any `badf-build`/`badf-git` file.\n\n## Tests (`tests/test_badf_verification_evidence.py`, failing-first)\n- `test_four_schemas_specialize_evidence_schema_and_close_the_binding` · `test_verification_record_schema_reuses_the_assurance_finding_item` · `test_typed_review_refuses_bare_pass_and_agent_observation` · `test_contract_result_maps_onto_outcome_and_indeterminate_never_passes` · `test_composed_binding_must_agree_with_the_artifact_tree` · `test_generic_g08_objects_stay_admissible` (WP-2026-0010 dossier unchanged) · `test_verify_refuses_invented_ballot_digest_and_duplicate_reviewer` · `test_verify_preserves_findings_across_synthesis` · `test_verify_matrix_rows_resolve_and_verified_rows_carry_no_open_major` · `test_verify_grants_no_authority` · `test_registry_pin_is_implemented`. Mutation: each control disabled → its test red.\n- Existing `test_badf_g08_verification`, `test_badf_engineering_verification_contract` (its \"no typed schema\" assertion flips to \"exists\", as BLD-A's did at BLD-B), self-dossier / reconcile / composition suites stay green.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Deterministic controls that judge typed objects against the Work Package and the composition record (target binding, staleness, independence quorum, runtime credit at dossier level, per-artifact non-coverage) — VER-C. Shadow — VER-D. Admission — VER-E. A verification ledger writer; `badf-security-assurance`.\n\n**Version tier:** minor (new schemas + subcommand, backward-compatible). **Lean mode:** advisory (structure only; the HARD-INVARIANT controls are C, disabled there). **Shared surface** (`badf_gate.py`, `schemas/`) → objects-level QA + REV by a non-authoring seat (BARCHI-2 or BARCHI-1) before merge.\n\n🛑 **STOP — awaiting operator approval of this plan** (covered by the #195 A→E authorization; recorded here for the ledger). No branch, no files, no registry edit until the id triple is re-confirmed with the other seats.\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
